# AegisForge review ownership -- ADVISORY, NOT BLOCKING.
#
# The branch ruleset sets require_code_owner_review = false, so nothing in
# this file can block a merge. Anyone on the team may open, review and merge
# any pull request, including their own, once the checks are green. The rule
# the team enforces is about pushing, not about reviewing: main and dev are
# never pushed to directly.
#
# What this file still does: GitHub automatically requests a review from the
# listed owner when a PR touches their paths. It is a "you probably want to
# look at this" signal for the areas where a wrong merge is expensive --
# governance, security, the wire protocol, the model catalogue, licensing.
# PRD 17.3 now matches this: reviews and CODEOWNERS are advisory, and the
# enforced rule is that nothing is pushed directly to main or dev.
#
# There is deliberately no global `*` owner, so ordinary PRs ping nobody.
#
# To turn this into a hard gate later, run:
#   REQUIRED_APPROVALS=1 ./scripts/setup-branch-protection.sh
# and set require_code_owner_review to true in that script.
#
